WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.110
It's 1999.

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:07.650
A new theme-park game is a hit, its parks
packed with guests riding and queuing,

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:08.970
all at once.

4
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.610
Its creator wrote almost all
of it in assembly language.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.170
Only 1 per cent was in C.

6
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.210
Most programmers would
call that the hard way.

7
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.530
So why would anyone build a whole
hit game in a language like that?

8
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.310
In this mission, you'll see that a
CPU can only execute machine code:

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.490
instructions in binary.

10
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.390
You'll meet assembly, which replaces
binary with short mnemonics,

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.870
one for each machine code instruction.

12
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.910
And you'll see why high-level
languages, with English-like keywords,

13
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.130
must be translated first.

14
00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.840
Your mission: work out why
its creator chose assembly.
